development.

44
00:02:21.850 --> 00:02:23.710
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:26.811
Which global issue do you think is the most serious?

46
00:02:28.117 --> 00:02:32.278
Clean water. Although the world is richer, many people still lack it.

47
00:02:33.583 --> 00:02:37.675
I agree. However, access to education is also important.

48
00:02:38.983 --> 00:02:42.704
True. Education helps development and reduces unemployment.

49
00:02:44.017 --> 00:02:46.875
Although there are many problems, peace gives us hope.

50
00:02:48.183 --> 00:02:50.987
Exactly. However, we all need to play our part.

51
00:02:52.283 --> 00:02:55.351
Grammar focus: Linking words: although · however.

52
00:02:55.651 --> 00:02:59.067
Use although to join two contrasting ideas in one sentence.

53
00:02:59.367 --> 00:03:02.690
Use however at the start of a new sentence, followed by a comma.

54
00:03:02.990 --> 00:03:06.710
For example: The city is rich. However, many people are poor.

55
00:03:07.010 --> 00:03:09.776
Put a comma after However at the start of a sentence.

56
00:03:10.783 --> 00:03:13.645
Now read and listen. Progress and Problems.

57
00:03:13.945 --> 00:03:17.082
The world has made great progress in the last fifty years.

58
00:03:18.383 --> 00:03:23.552
Although more children go to school than ever before, millions still have no access to education.

59
00:03:24.850 --> 00:03:29.311
Public health has improved; however, clean water is still a luxury in some areas.

60
00:03:30.617 --> 00:03:34.845
Population growth creates jobs, but it can also increase unemployment.

61
00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:40.518
Although these problems are big, peace and cooperation make solutions possible.

62
00:03:41.817 --> 00:03:44.295
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

63
